{"ts": "2026-10-27T05:35:36.078804Z", "run_id": "r-20261027T0505Z-eb94", "unit": "openspec:audit-queue-durable", "seq": 121, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-004", "id": "Q-004", "status": "answered", "reason": "Read packages/go/auditq/compact_test.go lines 332-392: TestDeadLetterMetrics uses a 422 sink, 3 events, asserts DeadLetterTotal()==3, DeadLetterFileSizeBytes()==os.Stat(wal+\".dead\").Size(), and that each line is JSON without the four forbidden keys. Read queue.go: isRejected covers 400/413/422 (line 809), settleRejected calls deadLetterWAL with \"rejected: HTTP %d\" (line 755), deadLetterWAL appends the record, increments deadLetterTotal and stores the file size (lines 500-524). Test assertions cover every clause of the scenario, so the criterion is covered and satisfied.", "called": true, "tasks": [], "target": "C-fad8c50f", "kind": "verdict", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.09199675, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "da638c5c17e4ff41da46385e36dc92db66ea6834ac1cecfe0f3a000904fde469", "checked": [{"ref": "packages/go/auditq/compact_test.go:332", "quote": "func TestDeadLetterMetrics(t *testing.T) {\n\tconst wantDeadLettered = 3", "claim": "The test enqueues exactly 3 events, the count the scenario names."}, {"ref": "packages/go/auditq/compact_test.go:336", "quote": "srv := httptest.NewServer(http.HandlerFunc(func(w http.ResponseWriter, _ *http.Request) {\n\t\tw.WriteHeader(http.StatusUnprocessableEntity)", "claim": "The sink answers 422 to every request, as the scenario's WHEN requires."}, {"ref": "packages/go/auditq/compact_test.go:360", "quote": "gotTotal := q.DeadLetterTotal()\n\tif gotTotal != int64(wantDeadLettered) {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"dead-letter counter: want %d got %d\", wantDeadLettered, gotTotal)", "claim": "The test fails unless DeadLetterTotal() is exactly 3."}, {"ref": "packages/go/auditq/compact_test.go:371", "quote": "if q.DeadLetterFileSizeBytes() != info.Size() {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"dead-letter file size gauge: want %d got %d\",", "claim": "The test fails unless DeadLetterFileSizeBytes() equals the stat size of <wal>.dead."}, {"ref": "packages/go/auditq/compact_test.go:383", "quote": "if err := json.Unmarshal([]byte(line), &m); err != nil {\n\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"dead-letter line is not valid JSON: %v\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor _, forbidden := range []string{\"credential\", \"api_key\", \"secret\", \"token_value\"} {", "claim": "Each dead-letter line must be JSON and must not hold any of the four forbidden keys."}, {"ref": "packages/go/auditq/queue.go:809", "quote": "func isRejected(status int) bool {\n\tswitch status {\n\tcase http.StatusBadRequest, http.StatusRequestEntityTooLarge, http.StatusUnprocessableEntity:\n\t\treturn true", "claim": "422 is treated as a refusal by the production code."}, {"ref": "packages/go/auditq/queue.go:755", "quote": "func (q *Queue) settleRejected(entry *batchEntry, status int) bool {\n\tq.deadLetterWAL(entry.event, fmt.Errorf(\"rejected: HTTP %d\", status))", "claim": "A refused event is dead-lettered with the required last_err text."}, {"ref": "packages/go/auditq/queue.go:519", "quote": "q.metrics.deadLetterTotal.Add(1)\n\n\t// Refresh dead-letter file size gauge.\n\tif info, statErr := os.Stat(path); statErr == nil {\n\t\tq.metrics.deadLetterFileSizeBytes.Store(info.Size())", "claim": "Each dead-letter append adds 1 to the counter and sets the file-size gauge to the file's size."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/audit-queue/spec.md#scenario-the-dead-letter-metrics-follow-refused-events", "quote": "**THEN** `DeadLetterTotal()` is 3, `DeadLetterFileSizeBytes()` equals the size of `<wal>.dead`, and each of its\n  lines is JSON without the keys `credential`, `api_key`, `secret` and `token_value`", "claim": "The scenario's three assertions are the ones the test checks."}]}
